sfactory conclusion given that it  was pretty directly tied to gohan's  character up killer found a new goal and  then he walked off into the sunset never  to be seen again  except for when he was briefly seen  again recommending biski to karapika but  more importantly killawatt was finally  able to achieve a solid sense of purpose  in regards to alaka and while no that  isn't a  tangible goal that one can really  achieve i do find it to be  an unfortunately satisfying conclusion  unfortunate because in my opinion more  kilowatt is never a bad thing in this  world but i will most certainly take an  ending like this because it could have  ended up significantly worse for him and  stepping into the more meta aspect of  hunter hunt for a second we are also  faced with the reality that we're on a  very bad path ourselves at the moment  where hunter hunter may never end and if  it does it's probably going to be within  the next arc or two  togashi's age and frequency of output  does not  necessarily allow for us to put kilowatt  back into the spotlight because we have  enough loose ends to tie up without  adding him back into the mix  so the way i tend to see things as that  gun and killua are both done  it's not that we'll never see them again  but they won't be major protagonists and  what's after this story is going to be  dedicated  to finishing off the characters of  karapika layorio and even hisoka  probably jing as well of course that is  just my opinion and there are many ways  that you could disagree with that  some of which we are about to explore  because if we do ignore hunter hunter's  publication  issues then there are indeed a variety  of ways in which kilowatt could see a  return as a protagonist because not 100  of things regarding him have been solved  i suppose the most obvious of which is  his relationship with illumi when we  last left these two illumi was scheming  to figure out a method by which to  control killua so that he could buy  proxy control alaka and thus have access  to the greatest power ever showcased in  this world  so one way that i could see a  satisfactory return of kilowatt is to  settle this conflict with illumi whether  it be through combat or another means  and i guess it would be nice to have  this come full circle because illumi is  kilawa's ultimate antagonist really and  he has been the specter lurking over him  for the large majority of hunter hunter  so why not have him directly confront  and overcome his brother the question i  will ask is is it necessary though  i would argue no but a lot of that  mindset comes from knowing what hunter  hunter is as a series  if this was any other shonen series i  would say 100  that kilauea needs to confront illumi  directly to have a satisfying ending but  this is hunter hunter and we cannot  treat it like a typical shonen because  plot points and foreshadowing are all  frequently abandoned  in favor of achieving a sense of realism  within the world  and what i mean by that is that you know  sometimes in real life you just don't  have your epic climactic conclusion  because that's life and hunter hunt has  made a point of invoking this realistic  approach on a number of occasions i mean  actually come to think of it one has  anything in hunt hunter ever ended in  that typical satisfactory manner that we  would see in many other shonens the  closest i can come is greed island where  against all odds gone did win the game  through a fun last minute bit of trivia  but in every other arc things tend to  end very suddenly  and not in the way that they were set up  to and this is also the main argument  that i would use against those who  insist that gon has to return because he  has unfinished business with hisoka  which is true but in this world that's  just not a good enough reason in my mind  and neither is killer's unfinished  business with illumi and to add to that  it's also entirely possible that illimi  will meet his own end during the current  arc because he is aboard the blackwell  one  and destined for a deadly date with  hisoka so if filmy is taken out during  this arc then well that's all the more  reason  the killer not to be brought back into  the fold there are still other arguments  so one of which is the gyro train of  thought and i have to say this every  time but look if you're an anime only  watcher this will probably confuse you a  bit because it was not  included in the 2011 adaptation but gyro  is a chimera ant who was stated by the  narrator of hunt hunter  to have some sort of destined meeting  with gon in the future and obviously  that has not happened at this point not  even in the manga but this serves as the  main driving force behind the insistence  that gone story isn't done  and there is a profound difference  between dismissing this and dismissing  something like i just stated before with  the whole hisoka rivalry which is that  togashi made a narrative point to state  that gon  and gyro will meet this isn't an  implication of an event or the desire of  a character expressed in speech  it was an inevitability stated by the  narrator of the story which is why i do  take it a lot more seriously but what  does that have to do with old killer  well it's because if there was any way  to bring him back into the action  a call from his old flame gone would  certainly do just that  if gon was ever in any trouble i have no  doubt that kilwa would race a godspeed  to his rescue and should we ever get to  a stage where it is time for this gyro  and gone business to actually play out i  guarantee you that gone is probably  going to be in a hell of a lot of  trouble but then again thoughts along  the sign generally assume that we will  ever get to much less conclude the dark  continent so this  is very much a dream at this stage but  kilauea could see a resurgence in other  ways  because even removing illumi from the  equation he is still zoltic and i highly  doubt that silver is just going 